him", 59.214, 59.304], ["nine", 59.304, 59.583], ["times", 59.583, 60.043], ["nothing", 60.24, 60.486], ["happens", 60.486, 60.921], ["turns", 61.109, 61.33], ["out", 61.33, 61.453], ["he's", 61.453, 61.552], ["not", 61.552, 61.733], ["a", 61.733, 61.774], ["zombie", 61.774, 62.217], ["that's", 62.388, 62.552], ["just", 62.552, 62.708], ["gary", 62.708, 63.308]], "lines": [[0.066, 5.631, "In this city, one bite turns you into a zombie. I'm the only kid who's immune. And whoever I touch turns back."], [5.885, 10.437, "I found out by accident. A zombie bit my arm, made a face, and said, \"Sorry about that.\""], [10.627, 14.552, "The grown-ups said, \"You're the cure. Stay in the bunker.\" They put me in a glass box."], [14.774, 15.611, "I left a pillow in it."], [15.813, 20.502, "Everyone thought I'd sneak out. I didn't. I took the ice cream truck. Zombies love the music."], [20.735, 23.525, "A hundred came running. I held out my hand for a high five."], [23.713, 26.961, "The baker. The bus driver. My math teacher. I did him last."], [27.184, 30.584, "Then I got bored of high fives. So I switched to tag. Then dodgeball."], [30.777, 33.519, "That's when the zombies figured it out. And they started running from me."], [33.695, 35.942, "Turns out they like being zombies. No school."], [36.165, 39.736, "They built a wall to keep me out. They put up a sign. Beware of kid."], [39.948, 42.182, "I'm ten, and I'm the scariest thing in the city."], [42.348, 44.326, "So I mailed myself over the wall in a box."], [44.539, 48.319, "The zombie in charge wore a yellow raincoat. My mom was always good at organizing."], [48.483, 51.818, "She ran. I caught her at the river. I didn't tag her. I hugged her."], [52.024, 54.222, "She blinked, and said, \"Why aren't you in the bunker?\""], [54.442, 57.095, "We walked home. Four thousand people walked behind us."], [57.314, 60.921, "There's one zombie left. I've high fived him nine times. Nothing happens."], [61.109, 63.308, "Turns out he's not a zombie. That's just Gary."]]}